4.3.text:
Ebymect is contraindicated in patients with:

-     hypersensitivity to the active substances or to any of the excipients listed in section 6.1;
-     any type of acute metabolic acidosis (such as lactic acidosis, diabetic ketoacidosis) (see section 4.4);
-     diabetic pre-coma;
-     severe renal failure (GFR < 30 mL/min) (see sections 4.2, 4.4 and 5.2);
-     acute conditions with the potential to alter renal function such as:
- dehydration,
- severe infection,
- shock;
-     acute or chronic disease which may cause tissue hypoxia such as:
- cardiac or respiratory failure,
- recent myocardial infarction,
- shock;
-     hepatic impairment (see sections 4.2, 4.4 and 5.2);
-     acute alcohol intoxication, alcoholism (see section 4.5).
